  {
    "source_id": "c5556444-b76f-5774-b94f-93b8f2189ca9",
    "complete_bank_replay": true,
    "field_type": "radio matches source",
    "bank_comparison": "all five choices, ignoring order",
    "checks": {
      ":question/problem": {
        "exact_normalized": false,
        "difference": [
          "- Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\right\\}.$",
          "?                                                  -----                            -------                                                                                      ------\n",
          "+ Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.$",
          "?                                                                                      ++++++++\n"
        ]
      },
      ":question/worked-solution": {
        "exact_normalized": false,
        "difference": [
          "  According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then ",
          "  ",
          "  $$",
          "  \\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.",
          "  $$",
          "  ",
          "  For the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. ",
          "  ",
          "  Also, since ",
          "  ",
          "  $$",
          "- \\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\right\\}",
          "?                 -----                                                                                                                                                                                                  ^^^^^^^\n",
          "+ \\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}",
          "?                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ^\n",
          "  $$",
          "  ",
          "  we conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$",
          "  ",
          "  Therefore,",
          "  ",
          "  $$",
          "  \\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}",
          "  $$"
        ]
      }
    },
    "accepted_presentation_changes": "Visible set braces may use fixed-size instead of scalable delimiters; algebraic terms are written in variable-index order. Independent coefficient parsing verifies equivalence; theorem, dimension-identification, expansion, substitution and final arithmetic stages are preserved."
  },
